          %h2#Theorems Theorems
          %p We discuss here formalizations and proofs of the relation/equivalence between various flavors of type theories and the corresponding flavors of categories.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#FirstOrderLogic"} First order logic and hyperdoctrines
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#DependentTypeTheory"} Dependent type theory and locally cartesian closed categories
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#HomotopyTypeTheory"} Homotopy type theory and locally cartesian closed (∞,1)-categories
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#HomotopyWithUnivalence"} Univalent homotopy type theory and elementary (∞,1)-toposes
          %h3#FirstOrderLogic First-order logic and hyperdoctrines
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cont
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cont
                  , that form a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+contexts"} category of contexts
                  of a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+logic"} first-order theory
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
